<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="What chudware.com and the Chudware desktop app collect and send: no accounts, no trackers, and a short list of network requests.">
  <div class="wrap legal-shell"><header><p class="eyebrow">Legal</p><h1>Privacy</h1><p class="effective">Effective October 22, 2026</p></header><div class="prose">
    <h2>This website</h2><p>chudware.com is a static website. It has no accounts, no forms, no analytics, and no advertising or tracking scripts. The hosting provider processes standard request data, such as IP addresses, to deliver pages and protect the site. Links to GitHub and other sites are governed by those sites' own policies.</p>
    <h2>The desktop app</h2><p>Chudware has no accounts and sends no telemetry. Your projects are saved as local files on your machine. The app contacts other services only in these cases:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Update checks.</strong> The app fetches the signed update manifest for your platform from the project's GitHub releases, and downloads an update from GitHub when one is available. GitHub receives the request under its own privacy terms.</li>
      <li><strong>AI providers you configure.</strong> When you use the copilot, the prompt, the project context, and the tool results needed for that turn go to the provider you selected, under that provider's terms. Provider credentials are stored on your machine and sent only to that provider.</li>
      <li><strong>Sites and downloads you request.</strong> Parts Library vendor searches, web lookups the copilot runs at your request, and optional components you install, such as the agent runtime or model weights, are fetched directly from the vendor's or publisher's site.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Chudware does not run a server that receives your projects, prompts, or credentials.</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2><p>Send privacy questions to <a href="mailto:support@chudware.com">support@chudware.com</a>. We will post material changes on this page and update the effective date.</p>
  </div></div>
</BaseLayout>
